## Summary
- [SUM-1] Scope: cross_section — the plan captures the broad goal but is not yet executor-ready; steps, repository references, and verification each have provable gaps.

## What Came Up Short
- [PA-001] Dimension: Executor Readiness | Defect: Executor research burden | Evidence: S-2 content only says update the review flow | Missing: exact policy, prompt, artifact, and routing edits | Cost: the executor will halt at S-2 to discover which files the change touches, blowing the run budget on framing instead of editing
- [PA-002] Dimension: Repository Accuracy | Defect: Repository reference invalid | Evidence: repository search finds no tests/test_planning_analysis.py | Missing: real target files and an existing test pattern to mirror | Cost: the executor will spend a discovery step verifying the missing path and likely write a stub test where none was planned
- [PA-003] Dimension: Verification Quality | Defect: Verification gap | Evidence: V-1 method is "run tests" | Missing: exact command and expected passing result | Cost: the executor cannot prove the change is verified and the analysis phase will reject the development_result on Plan Items Proven

## How To Fix
- [PA-001] Rewrite the S-2 step block so it names the exact policy, prompt, and artifact files plus the routing behavior to implement. Apply the revision through the standard stage/replace_all/finalize flow (see `## How To Fix` item 5).
- [PA-002] Rewrite the affected Steps and Critical Files entries so the nonexistent tests/test_planning_analysis.py reference is replaced with real target files and an existing test file whose pattern should be mirrored.
- [PA-003] Rewrite the Verification section with exact commands such as `uv run pytest -q tests/test_policy_loader.py` and name the expected passing evidence, then resubmit the document.
